  "facts": [
    "The Franklin Delano Roosevelt Mid‑Hudson Bridge, completed in 1930, was the world’s sixth‑longest suspension bridge at opening, spanning 3,000 feet with a 135‑foot clearance over the Hudson.",
    "Designed by Polish engineer Ralph Modjeski, the bridge’s stiffening trusses sit atop the deck—a rare construction choice that distinguishes it from most suspension bridges.",
    "In 2009, composer Joseph Bertolozzi turned the Mid‑Hudson Bridge into a musical instrument, recording its vibrations for a Billboard‑charting CD titled \"Bridge Music.\""
